WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.334 --> 00:00:13.238
Several weeks passed.

2
00:00:13.239 --> 00:00:17.501
One morning Mowgli climbed onto Rama's back.

3
00:00:17.502 --> 00:00:21.521
Rama was the largest male in the herd of buffalo.

4
00:00:21.522 --> 00:00:28.938
The other animals began following Rama.

5
00:00:28.939 --> 00:00:33.793
"Graze the cattle on your own today," Mowgli said to the other children.

6
00:00:33.794 --> 00:00:38.427
"I'm going to stay with the buffalo."

7
00:00:38.428 --> 00:00:42.173
Mowgli led the buffalo to the edge of the plain.

8
00:00:42.174 --> 00:00:45.324
That was where the river came out of the jungle.

9
00:00:45.325 --> 00:00:50.220
Then he dropped off Rama's back and ran toward the bamboo.

10
00:00:50.221 --> 00:00:54.522
Gray Brother was waiting there, just as Mowgli had hoped.

11
00:00:54.523 --> 00:00:57.914
They greeted one another happily.

12
00:00:57.915 --> 00:01:01.410
But Gray Brother looked worried.

13
00:01:01.411 --> 00:01:05.579
"Shere Khan came back to the jungle to wait for you.

14
00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:08.799
There was little food, so he left.

15
00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:11.408
He will come back soon, Mowgli.

16
00:01:11.409 --> 00:01:16.238
And this time he will kill you."

17
00:01:16.239 --> 00:01:21.917
"When the tiger returns, wait for me in the ravine near the flowering tree."

18
00:01:21.918 --> 00:01:25.226
Mowgli pointed to a rock across the plain.

19
00:01:25.227 --> 00:01:33.091
"Until then, sit on that rock, where I can see you."

20
00:01:33.092 --> 00:01:36.193
Every day Mowgli herded the buffalo.

21
00:01:36.194 --> 00:01:41.667
Day after day he saw Gray Brother sitting on the rock across the plain.

22
00:01:41.668 --> 00:01:49.385
Most days Mowgli just lay on the grass, listening carefully to the sounds as Father Wolf had taught him.

23
00:01:49.386 --> 00:01:55.932
If Shere Khan approached, Mowgli would surely hear him in the stillness.

24
00:01:55.933 --> 00:02:00.270
One day Mowgli glanced at the rock.

25
00:02:00.271 --> 00:02:03.002
It was empty.

26
00:02:03.003 --> 00:02:10.477
Quickly he herded the buffalo to the tree with the golden red flowers.

27
00:02:10.478 --> 00:02:13.169
There sat Gray Brother.

28
00:02:13.170 --> 00:02:16.419
Every hair on his back was standing up.

29
00:02:16.420 --> 00:02:20.974
"Shere Khan has been hiding for a month," Gray Brother said.

30
00:02:20.975 --> 00:02:25.394
"But last night he crossed the plains with Tabaqui."

31
00:02:25.395 --> 00:02:28.599
Mowgli frowned. "Tabaqui?"

32
00:02:28.600 --> 00:02:31.571
Mowgli was not afraid of Shere Khan.

33
00:02:31.572 --> 00:02:35.356
However, Tabaqui was another story.

34
00:02:35.357 --> 00:02:38.479
The jackal was very cunning.

35
00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:49.163
"Have no fear. I met Tabaqui at dawn—and took care of him." Gray Brother licked his lips.

36
00:02:49.164 --> 00:02:52.299
"First he gave me some important information.

37
00:02:52.300 --> 00:02:56.877
Shere Khan plans to wait for you at the village gate tonight."

38
00:02:56.878 --> 00:03:01.090
"Where's Shere Khan now?" Mowgli asked.

39
00:03:01.091 --> 00:03:05.930
"He's in the big, dry ravine. The one along the river."

40
00:03:05.931 --> 00:03:09.367
"Has he hunted yet today?" Mowgli asked.

41
00:03:09.368 --> 00:03:13.229
The answer could mean his own life or death.

42
00:03:13.230 --> 00:03:18.001
"He ate a large meal at dawn," Gray Brother replied.

43
00:03:18.002 --> 00:03:21.366
"Good." Mowgli was thinking aloud.

44
00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:25.000
"That means he'll be too full to move fast.

45
00:03:25.001 --> 00:03:29.495
If there were more of us, we could attack him.

46
00:03:29.496 --> 00:03:33.918
But these buffalo will not charge unless they smell him.

47
00:03:33.919 --> 00:03:38.687
And I cannot speak their language yet to explain things to them.

48
00:03:38.688 --> 00:03:41.860
Do you think we can pick up the tiger's scent?

49
00:03:41.861 --> 00:03:44.962
That way the buffalo can smell it."

50
00:03:44.963 --> 00:03:47.412
Gray Brother shook his head.

51
00:03:47.413 --> 00:03:52.449
"Shere Khan traveled in the river. This leaves no scent."

52
00:03:52.450 --> 00:03:55.686
"Tabaqui must have told him to do that.

53
00:03:55.687 --> 00:03:59.329
Shere Khan would not have thought of it alone."

54
00:03:59.330 --> 00:04:04.203
Mowgli stood with his finger in his mouth.

55
00:04:04.204 --> 00:04:09.579
"I can take the buffalo through the jungle to the head of the ravine.

56
00:04:09.580 --> 00:04:14.580
We can block that end . . . but Shere Khan will escape the other way.

57
00:04:14.581 --> 00:04:18.261
We must block the other end too."

58
00:04:18.262 --> 00:04:20.695
Mowgli looked at the wolf.

59
00:04:20.696 --> 00:04:24.865
"Can you take half of the animals and do that?"

60
00:04:24.866 --> 00:04:30.204
"Not by myself, but . . . I have brought a wise helper."

61
00:04:30.205 --> 00:04:34.453
Gray Brother ran off and dropped into a hole.

62
00:04:34.454 --> 00:04:38.136
Seconds later a gray head popped up.

63
00:04:38.137 --> 00:04:42.618
The hot air filled with a familiar hunting howl.

64
00:04:42.619 --> 00:04:50.042
Mowgli clapped his hands in delight. "Akela!"
